// # oodar/docs/archive/changes_v1_v3.oot — Historical Changelog Archive (v1.0.0–v3.4.2)
//
// Logline: Historical release log of legacy oodar runtime versions from v1.0.0 through v3.4.2, sorted in strict descending semantic version order.
//
// Setup: Referenced by active oodar/CHANGES.md. Preserves structural changes, capability sweeps, and security audits.
//
// Beats:
//   1. v3.4.x releases: Cap helper relocations, timing tests, QA test hardening.
//   2. v3.3.x releases: Bitmask subset checks, path attenuators, OTP supervision fixes.
//   3. v3.2.x releases: Fail-closed memory reads, adversarial scanners, token derivation.
//   4. v3.0.x–v3.1.x releases: Security defect closures, public mutator cap-gating, MetricsCap.
//   5. v1.x–v2.x releases: 256-line file split, zero-trust audits, baseline host runtime.

## v3.4.2 — 2026-09-06: Cryptographic Timing Verification
- Integrated dudect constant-time leakage tests for capability-protected crypto routines.
- Confirmed timing variation satisfies statistical bounds (|t| < 4.5).

## v3.4.1 — 2026-09-06: QA Test Harness Hardening
- Extended regression tests in `qa/` for edge cases in memory and string handling.
- Hardened test runner execution against transient signal aborts.

## v3.4.0 — 2026-09-06: Capability Subsystem Refactoring
- Relocated capability attenuation routines into `sec/cap/cap_attenuate_hmac.c`.
- Relocated allocation, time, and FFI capability gates to dedicated `sec/cap/` files.
- Cleaned up event bus placement by moving metrics from `app/` to `core/event/`.

## v3.3.4 — 2026-09-05: Concurrency and Test Hardening
- Fixed TOCTOU race in `oo_otp_supervise` by locking actor boot state during restart checks.
- Corrected test harness ordering in `tests_challenger_cap_escape.c` for `oo_proc_mem_read`.

## v3.3.3 — 2026-09-05: Path Capability Memory Fix
- Implemented deep-copy semantics for path capability structures.
- Resolved memory corruption and use-after-free conditions on capability attenuation.

## v3.3.2 — 2026-09-05: MLKEM Buffer Boundary Fix
- Resolved stringop-overread defect in MLKEM `k_prf` key generation routines.
- Bound checked internal buffer indexing to prevent out-of-bounds reads.

## v3.3.1 — 2026-09-05: Path Attenuation Verification
- Enforced path-prefix normalization and directory traversal rejection.
- Authored contract test suites verifying fail-closed attenuation behavior.

## v3.3.0 — 2026-09-05: Capability Bitmask Subset Enforcement
- Enforced Rule 2 bitmask subset invariants during capability attenuation.
- Asserted that child capability tokens cannot exceed parent permission sets.

## v3.2.3 — 2026-09-05: Fuzzing Smoke Suite Integration
- Added fuzzing smoke tests verifying parser robustness against malformed payloads.
- Verified absence of panics and unhandled memory faults on random inputs.

## v3.2.2 — 2026-09-05: Differential Capability Derivation
- Added differential test suites comparing capability derivation algorithms.
- Confirmed exact match across token hashing and rights calculation.

## v3.2.1 — 2026-09-05: Adversarial File Scanning
- Integrated adversarial reading scanner testing non-standard file descriptors.
- Asserted fail-closed rejection on invalid permissions and unauthorized descriptors.

## v3.2.0 — 2026-09-05: Process Memory Safety Hardening
- Enforced fail-closed ordering in `oo_proc_mem_read` prior to Landlock checks.
- Prevented unauthorized process memory reads on missing or invalid capability tokens.

## v3.1.0 — 2026-09-04: Security Defect Remediation
- Fixed GPU capability shadowing defect in `oo_gpu_hip_try_launch_dispatch`.
- Removed pseudo-random LCG fallbacks; enforced fail-closed entropy requirements.
- Standardized UDP socket binding to require `BindCap`.

## v3.0.0 — 2026-09-04: Public Mutator Capability Gating
- Gated 8 public mutators (`oo_read_stdin`, `oo_file_stamp`, `oo_metrics_*`) behind capabilities.
- Re-introduced `MetricsCap` at bit `0x800` to secure process-global telemetry.
- Expanded capability token inventory to 26 total substrate capabilities.

## v2.3.0 — 2026-09-03: Architectural 256-Line File Enforcement
- Partitioned 17 monolithic files into 60+ modular units across 9 directories.
- Maintained exact binary ABI equivalence with zero public symbol signature alterations.
- Isolated FIPS 203/204 mathematical engines (`mldsa_internal.c`, `mlkem_internal.c`).

## v2.2.0 — 2026-09-03: Zero-Trust Security Audit Pass 3
- Closed 5 security defects and 4 governance gaps across filesystem and memory subsystems.
- Tightened Landlock sandbox rules for temporary file operations.

## v2.1.0 — 2026-09-02: Zero-Trust Security Audit Pass 2
- Remedied 6 critical and 11 moderate security issues across IPC and network stacks.
- Reserved bit `0x800` to prevent future token allocation collisions.

## v2.0.0 — 2026-09-01: Memory Allocation Capability Protection
- Gated memory allocation and weak reference operations behind explicit capability tokens.
- Deprecated legacy unmanaged memory mutation primitives.

## v1.0.1 — 2026-08-25: Internal Subsystem Reorganization
- Reorganized internal directory structures and unified build scripts.
- Migrated legacy test fixtures into standard `qa/` challenger suites.

## v1.0.0 — 2026-08-20: Sovereign Runtime Substrate Baseline
- Initial stable release of the `oodar` C99 runtime substrate.
- Integrated Landlock sandboxing, capability-based security, and core POSIX abstractions.
